WEBVTT

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.380
That's Theo Cornaro?

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.380
He's much younger than I thought!

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.890
To launch an attack on Ladvan Torius' castle,

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.350
we'll first need to
successfully capture that town.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:25.310
If a battle ensues, both sides are
sure to see heavy casualties.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.030
That youth is the one
who defeated the Waldlind knights?

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.280
What will become of our town?

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.910
It would be better to avoid a battle, huh?

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.170
But their leader, Lord Ladvan,
is a man of conscience.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.920
No matter what you propose,
I'm sure he won't surrender.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.800
But Sir Theo, maybe you can...

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.390
Now this is just the next-best plan...

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.390
If he refuses to surrender, please convince
him to settle things outside the village.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.480
As a man who values his people,
I'm sure he'll comply.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.790
I am the leader of this village, Ladvan Torius!

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:58.380
I am a knight serving Villar Constance,
the Earl of Artuk...

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.680
Theo Cornaro!

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:05.470
I've agreed to meet with you,
but my mind is already made up.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:10.940
If it's my court rank and land you desire,
I will take you on, but only in battle.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:14.820
In other words, you're swearing
allegiance to the Alliance?

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.400
I plan to offer Lady Marrine Kreische
my pledge of fealty down the road.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:21.700
Is that so?

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:24.990
With so many townspeople here to defend you,

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.870
I have no hope of defeating you
with my troops alone.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.830
I do not wish to harm your people in a battle.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:35.090
I can see why you're renowned as a hero.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.210
In that case, I advise you to leave now.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.470
That's my intention.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.970
But before I go,
I have one question for you.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.640
Is this the victory that you seek?

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.600
That should be more than obvious.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.020
Sooner or later, the great Union army
will arrive to attack this town.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.730
I was able to survive this long.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.820
Even if I withdraw,

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:04.990
Lassic David, the King of Sievis,
is sure to attack with his force of 30,000 men.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:05.870
30,000?

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:07.910
We wouldn't stand a chance!

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.170
If you wish to become
the true victor in all this,

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:15.840
I suggest that you lead your men
from the castle to attack.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:17.630
Oh?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.130
In doing so, your loyalty to
the Alliance will remain unscathed,

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.180
and your people won't have to suffer.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.020
If I can go down holding my own
against the hero Theo Cornaro,

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.430
I will die a happy man.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.020
Allow me to die as a victor.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.070
No, that won't do!

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:40.400
We are prepared to fight
by your side, Lord Ladvan!

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.490
Isn't that right, everybody?
Isn't that right?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.490
Right! That's right!

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:52.160
If I die, this battle will come to an end.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.420
There's no need for you to sacrifice your lives.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.720
Lord Ladvan...

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.680
What we want is for you
to continue ruling this town.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.100
We'll follow you wherever you go!

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.060
Who cares if we're with
the Alliance or the Union?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.690
We will protect you, Lord Ladvan!

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:15.520
Lord Ladvan!

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:18.610
Our leader!

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.240
It looks like I've lost here.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:28.160
You're every inch the valiant Lord
I thought you'd be.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.990
And that's why I'd like to ask you...

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.330
Would you consider joining me in defeat?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.170
Join you in defeat?

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:40.880
I'm asking you to value your people's trust,
rather than your loyalty to the Alliance.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:44.920
You mean I should be true to my people,
rather than be their Lord?

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.800
That's precisely what I see as the ideal Lord.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.530
Everyone, I must ask for your forgiveness.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.080
I intend to leave the Alliance,
and switch sides to the Union.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:16.460
I choose to live my life alongside all of you.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.100
I leave my fate entirely in your hands.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.600
All I ask is that you guarantee
my people's survival and their fortunes.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.480
Understood.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:40.610
I'm sure Sir Lassic
will give you a warm welcome.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.400
How unfortunate for you.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.110
If only I'd vacated my castle,
it would've been such a coup for you,

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:50.530
and you could've taken my Crest.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.120
I don't care for military feats.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.500
What matters is that there were
no senseless casualties.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.460
Looks like I had the wrong read on you.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:09.680
So many Lords obsess only
about gaining more land or Crests,

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.510
yet you show concern for not only
your own people, but your enemy's as well.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:17.930
I can see that you're a man
who truly adheres to the code of Lords.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:22.310
Rather than Lord Lassic,
I would like to serve under you!

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:29.530
I am currently a man serving under Lord Villar.
I cannot accept your pledge of allegiance.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:34.450
Then, until the time comes,
will you entrust your Crest to me?

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:38.410
Very well.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:43.040
I'll be sure to welcome you as a loyal Lord.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.050
Unbelievable.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:58.930
Never mind surrendering,
he actually promised to serve him!

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:31.090
Lord Lassic has defeated Jericho Orlick,
the King of Forbes.

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:35.550
Who knew he'd only take
five days to conquer Forbes?

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:40.230
Thanks to him, the King of Clovis
surrendered his castle without any prodding.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.730
Without us losing a single soldier, that is.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:52.070
I believe both Sir Milza and Sir Theo's exploits
have shattered the enemy's morale.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:55.240
Both feats were extraordinary.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.740
And both were carried out true to form,
wouldn't you say?

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:09.840
Glory to the Union!
Lord Villar, Earl of Artuk!

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.060
The road to Jalucia has been paved!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.270
I thank you all for your hard work!

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:37.280
After declining his request for aid,
I knew this might happen, but...

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.580
Theo Cornaro, eh?

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:46.540
Milza Kuces didn't even need a day to seize
the castle of one of our more dominant Lords.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:47.920
Milza?

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:51.250
Isn't he the son of the Viceroy of Dartania?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.550
So how are our Lords taking all this?

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.590
Many of them are distraught.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:58.470
I'm sure they are.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:03.560
With Sievis lost, and not knowing how
the neighboring Lords will react,

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.140
Waldlind can ill afford to send backup troops.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.570
Even so, I'm sure that some
will criticize what I do.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.610
Keep your eyes on those Lords!

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.030
Understood.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.340
Out of place, huh?

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:35.840
Out of place, indeed.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.590
I wonder where Lord Alexis is?

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:40.600
Do you think he'll dance with us?

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:42.850
Earl of Artuk, is that you?

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.980
That's the Earl of Le Couleurs,
Lord Klute Gallas.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.730
You took so long to show up, I was worried!

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:53.530
Well, our path here was blocked.

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:57.610
Normally, we would've given you
a proper hero's welcome.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:01.490
But some of the Lords here
aren't thrilled with what you've accomplished.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:08.000
Unfortunately, my cousin seems to be set on
taking out the Union with military might.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:16.260
So we must not give Marrine
ample time to do that!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:20.640
If we advance into the Alliance at full strength,
and conquer Waldlind,

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:23.010
we can finish them off for good!

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.270
Yes, that's the spirit!

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:31.310
It's been a long time, Marquis Dawson.

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:34.020
I commend you for your prowess in battle,

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:37.530
but didn't I notify you about
suspending hostilities with the Alliance?

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.360
Why didn't you follow the consensus?

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:42.660
If you're calling it a consensus,

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:46.620
then you should've
consulted me before sending it out.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.710
Meaning you'll go along with whatever
is decided at this Lords' Congress, right?

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.540
I'm sure I'll have no other choice.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:56.050
Whatever happens,

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.510
don't forget the words you just uttered!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:10.310
Do most of the Lords here actually believe
that the current peace will last forever?

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:11.940
It can't be helped.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.560
Ever since that battle against
the Alliance thirty years ago,

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:18.320
only Artuk and its surrounding areas
have seen battle.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:22.030
And that's why this conference
is a once-in-a-lifetime chance!

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:23.950
Villar, Earl of Artuk!

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.620
Tell them what a threat the Alliance is,

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:30.330
and that to survive, our only option
is to mount a full-scale war!

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:34.040
This is not going to be
a tranquil meeting for me.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:37.130
The Marquis of Jalucia, Lord Alexis...

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:38.920
Entering!

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.280
Lord Villar!

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:07.950
Thank you so much
for making the long trip here.

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:09.740
No, no...

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:15.250
I would cross the entire continent
if it meant getting an audience with you.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:18.040
And you're...

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:24.010
You saved me from peril
in the Great Hall. I thank you!

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:28.430
Please forgive me for failing
to save both archdukes.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:30.850
Then you're...

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:32.730
Are you Sir Theo?

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.020
It's an honor to meet you, sir.

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:38.020
I knew it was you!

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:40.400
I've been wanting to have a nice,
long chat with you!

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:45.410
Since it's not possible to do that here,
allow me to arrange a meeting sometime!

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:47.570
I'm not worthy of your kind words, sir.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:49.280
<i>Though it's probably lip-service.</i>

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.670
Theo? Siluca?

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:02.630
What is it?

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:06.180
I've spotted someone I must introduce you to.

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:10.930
I haven't seen you
since the last Lords' Congress...

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:13.020
Lord Pederico Rossini!

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.350
Well, well, the Earl of Artuk.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:21.190
This young knight here
hails from Sistina, you see.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:22.030
Ah...

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:29.700
My name... is Theo Cornaro.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.410
Did you say Cornaro?

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:36.670
Was that name handed down to you
by your forebears?

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:38.960
No, I am a commoner.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:43.670
When becoming a Lord, I took on a name
closely connected to my homeland.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:46.880
Cornaro is a prestigious name in Sistina.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:51.930
Not to be assumed on a whim
by a commoner Lord.

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:53.770
You should take another name.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:55.180
It wasn't a whim.

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:58.810
Since I intend to return
to my homeland someday.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:05.190
Sistina is an island in the demon world.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:08.320
If you go back, no good will come out of it.

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:11.240
That's for me to decide, sir.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.630
What a day we had, huh?

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.090
I agree.

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.590
Shall we have some tea?

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:31.470
It's unusual for Irvin
not to show up at a time like this.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:36.930
Looks like we have company.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.850
Someone of significantly high rank.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:44.150
But Lord Villar is still
at the Marquis of Jalucia's castle...

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:52.120
Theo, you have a guest!
Someone named Alexis.

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.240
Alexis...

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:55.410
Huh?

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.580
Everyone's been ordered not to enter.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.630
Because I wanted to talk to you
with no one else around.

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:07.460
It's an honor, sir.
But I'm also perplexed.

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:11.970
We're not of sufficient rank
to speak with you in person.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.890
Oh, I only inherited my court rank
from my father.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:19.890
But you, Sir Theo,
strengthened your Crest on your own,

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:24.020
became the former ruler of Sievis,
and even reached the rank of viscount.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:27.030
Well, I certainly didn't
accomplish that on my own.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:30.030
It was all thanks to Siluca here,
and my comrades.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:34.120
Above all, if Lord Villar hadn't come to my aid,

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.910
I wouldn't have survived.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:40.080
And the court rank and lands
you risked your life to acquire...

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:43.170
I hear you gave them up for Lady Siluca
without a second thought?

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:48.170
It was Siluca who guided me
when I was nothing but a wanderer.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.930
Even if it came at the cost of all else,
I have no regrets.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:56.430
When I heard that story, I was deeply moved.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:59.060
To choose love over
one's court rank and land...

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.060
If only I had the courage to do so.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.650
All I did was choose
what was most important to me.

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:12.950
In my case, my love for Marrine
is more important than anything else.

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:15.740
When I realized that it wasn't meant to be,

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.790
I even considered ending my life.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:25.880
But Marrine has forged a path for
us to be united.

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:26.710
And yet...

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.460
I still love Marrine, even now.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:36.720
So much that I'd give up my court rank
and lands if it meant we could be together!

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:41.220
I understand how you feel, but you can't...

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:43.850
Yes, I'm aware.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:48.480
Marrine is a woman who
takes her responsibilities seriously.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:52.740
I'm sure she'll steadfastly try
to fulfill her role as leader of the Alliance.

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:57.740
I hear Lady Marrine still dresses in black
and continues to mourn.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:00.540
I'm sure her resolve is ironclad.

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:07.040
My wish is for all Lords across the continent
to cease fighting and unite.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:10.880
And then we can hold a meeting
to choose our emperor.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.340
That way, there will be
no more war on the continent,

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.380
and the era of Chaos will come to an end.

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:25.270
That's everything I wanted
to talk to you about.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:29.650
And I also want you two to find happiness.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:35.280
So you can show the world that there are more
important things than court rank or territories.

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:37.700
We give you our promise.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.950
At present, I am serving the Earl of Artuk.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:50.290
But aside from that relationship, I will do
everything I can to make your wish come true.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:55.340
So that one day,
you and Lady Marrine can be united.

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:58.430
And so the continent will become one.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:02.180
Thank you!

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:12.730
When we're not in the public eye,
I hope you'll think of me as your friend.

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:14.820
I know I'll be thinking of you as mine.

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:16.610
Understood.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:20.070
- I would love to stay, but I must return to...
- We're under attack

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:21.570
Everyone, please watch your backs!

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:29.750
Wall, O Wall!
Nothing on this earth can hope to scale it!

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:49.940
Lord Alexis!

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:55.900
Who are these guys?

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:02.320
Omerta...

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:04.740
This is Rossini's flag.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:08.160
No one who accepts it can go against orders.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:11.750
No matter how cruel the action may be,
he'll carry it out without remorse.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.540
Then what's the enemy after?

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:25.430
Parry!

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:36.480
Thank you, sir!

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:39.780
No need to thank me.

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:51.830
Lady Siluca...

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:54.460
What's going on?
Not being here when we needed you...

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.340
Please forgive me.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:20:59.260
You were being targeted by snipers.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:04.760
And there was a Shadow among them,
holding me back...

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:06.640
Most likely, it was an assassin.

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:07.850
Did you kill it?

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:09.850
It got away from me.

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:17.860
You were all exposed to danger because of me.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.110
I'm so sorry...

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:35.710
I was the target, wasn't I?

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:38.130
Even if it was mistaken identity,

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:41.670
an assassination attempt on a marquis
is far from a minor offense.

